+## 10a. FastLED Patterns (local fork)
+
+A FastLED Pattern is detected by `patternLanguage(src)` (`src/engine/patternLanguage.ts`): the leading comment block (at most 20 lines) carries `// @pxlblz-language fastled`. No schema change; `isFastLedSource` guards every Pixelblaze-only path (Send to Controller gate and push, saved-artifact reconciliation, saved-program matching, Show pickers and `compileShowForPreview` / v2 stage preparation via `showFastLedGuard.ts`, agent discovery, Copy/.epe).
+
+- Compile: `fastledStore` posts `{source, defines}` to the FastLED compile service (`fastledCompileClient.ts`, override `?fastledService=`), caches `WebAssembly.Module`s per (source, defines) and publishes `previewSource` only after a successful compile of the still-current buffer of the same Pattern; errors set `compileStatus` broken and become Monaco markers (owner `fastled`). Offline: `serviceStatus` offline, retry with backoff, `compileStatus` untouched.
+- Preview: `Preview.tsx` resolves the layout with the `@pxlblz-dim` dimension, passes `PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS` (and `PXLBLZ_WIDTH/HEIGHT` for regular grids), instantiates the vendored host (`src/engine/fastled/fastledWasmHost.ts`, ABI 1) and drives `createFastLedPatternHandle` through the shared `startLoop` (fast shim always). `beforeRender(dt)` runs `frame(dt)`; `render*(i)` emits byte/255 of L2 wire bytes (default, RGB order after brightness/correction/dither) or L1 `leds[]`. byte/255 → `Math.round(v*255)` is exact, so the packed frame and the router receive FastLED's bytes (golden test: 0 differing bytes against the native FastLED reference).
+- Controls: FastLED UI elements map to ranged slider/toggle Controls (`PatternMetadata.controls[].range`); values persist in `PatternRecord.controls` (`controls_json`) keyed by UI name.
+- Limits: main-thread wasm; the host's loop/show budget catches runaway loops that call `millis/delay/show`, but a pure `while(true){}` still freezes the tab. Playlists (sequencing Pixelblaze and FastLED Patterns with cuts/crossfades) are a planned follow-up.
+
